  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **2000-05-14t01-Squelch The Weasel**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **2000-05-14t02-Captain Fantasy**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **2000-05-14t03-Never Squeal**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **2000-05-14t04-Even If You Don't**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **2000-05-14t05-Buckingham Green**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **2000-05-14t06-Stallion Pt. 3**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **2000-05-14t07-Roses Are Free**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **2000-05-14t08-Flute Of The Chi**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2000-05-14** (recommended): soundboard; 30 songs; 147 min [1]\n- **ween2000-05-14-flac16**: source not stated; 30 songs; 153 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]. Said about its sound: Taper says the recording sounds poor because the mics sat near the soundboard, with crowd noise intruding [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Mics were placed in front of the soundboard on the path between bar and bathrooms; taper guarded them all show [3]\n- The crowd was very drunk, stumbling into the mic stand and shouting into the microphones [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2000-05-14**: source: SBD>?>cdr [1]\n- **ween2000-05-14-flac16**: taped by morst; transferred by morst; source: Neumann KM140's > DAT [2]. Also: Recorded with Neumann SKM140 mics in x/y on a stand, through a Beyer MV-100 preamp; Captured to a Sony TCD-10 Pro II DAT recorder at 48kHz, then transferred onward from DAT [2]",
